{
 "source": "trapp",
 "book": "EXO",
 "chapter": 29,
 "units": [
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.1",
   "range": "EXO.29.1",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "30698fef",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.1#p1-30698fef",
     "text": "All sorts of sacrifices - sin offerings, burnt offerings, peace offerings - were to be offered for the priests, because of the special holiness and honour of their calling.",
     "anchor": "Take one young bullock."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.2",
   "range": "EXO.29.2",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "59df1281",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.2#p1-59df1281",
     "text": "See 1Co 5:7-8. {See Trapp on \"1Co 5:7\"} {See Trapp on \"1Co 5:8\"]",
     "anchor": "And unlevened bread.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Co 5:7-8",
       "ref": "1CO.5.7-8"
      },
      {
       "text": "1Co 5:7",
       "ref": "1CO.5.7"
      },
      {
       "text": "1Co 5:8",
       "ref": "1CO.5.8"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.4",
   "range": "EXO.29.4",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "f56794fc",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.4#p1-f56794fc",
     "text": "A type of Christ’s baptism. {Mat 3:13-17}",
     "anchor": "Wash them with water.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 3:13-17",
       "ref": "MAT.3.13-17"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.6",
   "range": "EXO.29.6",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "0cc8856d",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.6#p1-0cc8856d",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"Exo 28:40\"}",
     "anchor": "The holy crown.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Exo 28:40",
       "ref": "EXO.28.40"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.7",
   "range": "EXO.29.7",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "8d6a13e8",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.7#p1-8d6a13e8",
     "text": "Typing out that abundance of the Holy Spirit poured upon Christ, {Isa 61:1} and upon Christions. {1Jn 2:27 Psa 133:2}",
     "anchor": "The Anointing oil.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Isa 61:1",
       "ref": "ISA.61.1"
      },
      {
       "text": "1Jn 2:27",
       "ref": "1JN.2.27"
      },
      {
       "text": "Psa 133:2",
       "ref": "PSA.133.2"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.8",
   "range": "EXO.29.8",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "0cc8856d",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.8#p1-0cc8856d",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"Exo 28:40\"}",
     "anchor": "Coats, &c.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Exo 28:40",
       "ref": "EXO.28.40"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.9",
   "range": "EXO.29.9",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "e3612b74",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.9#p1-e3612b74",
     "text": "Heb., Fill their hands, sc., with sacrifices: they were not to fill their own hands, as Jeroboam’s priests did. {1Ki 13:33, margin; Heb 5:5}",
     "anchor": "Consecrate.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ki 13:33",
       "ref": "1KI.13.33"
      },
      {
       "text": "Heb 5:5",
       "ref": "HEB.5.5"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.10",
   "range": "EXO.29.10",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "9ea3bed2",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.10#p1-9ea3bed2",
     "text": "As transferring the guilt of their sins upon Christ. {Isa 53:6}",
     "anchor": "Shall put their hands.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Isa 53:6",
       "ref": "ISA.53.6"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.11",
   "range": "EXO.29.11",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "7d353c7d",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.11#p1-7d353c7d",
     "text": "Pointing to Christ, the door into heaven. {Heb 10:20 Joh 10:9}",
     "anchor": "By the door.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Heb 10:20",
       "ref": "HEB.10.20"
      },
      {
       "text": "Joh 10:9",
       "ref": "JHN.10.9"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.12",
   "range": "EXO.29.12",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "17c46b77",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.12#p1-57b98745",
     "text": "For \"without blood there was no remission of sin.\" {Heb 9:22}",
     "anchor": "The blood of the bullock.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Heb 9:22",
       "ref": "HEB.9.22"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.12#p2-acbc31c8",
     "text": "To signify the plenteous redemption wrought by Christ.",
     "anchor": "Beside the bottom of the altar."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.13",
   "range": "EXO.29.13",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "49cbf401",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.13#p1-49cbf401",
     "text": "God must have the very best of the best; since Christ offered himself, and the best parts he had.",
     "anchor": "All the fat that covereth."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.14",
   "range": "EXO.29.14",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "6026e63d",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.14#p1-6026e63d",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"Heb 13:12\"} {See Trapp on \"Heb 7:27\"} {See Trapp on \"Heb 7:28\"}",
     "anchor": "Without the camp.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Heb 13:12",
       "ref": "HEB.13.12"
      },
      {
       "text": "Heb 7:27",
       "ref": "HEB.7.27"
      },
      {
       "text": "Heb 7:28",
       "ref": "HEB.7.28"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.15",
   "range": "EXO.29.15",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "d19f657a",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.15#p1-d19f657a",
     "text": "After the sin offering, other offerings: till sin be expiated, no service is accepted.",
     "anchor": "Thou shalt also take."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.16",
   "range": "EXO.29.16",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "787e8be3",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.16#p1-787e8be3",
     "text": "See 1Pe 1:2.",
     "anchor": "Sprinkle it.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Pe 1:2",
       "ref": "1PE.1.2"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.17",
   "range": "EXO.29.17",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "b4dff0a0",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.17#p1-b4dff0a0",
     "text": "This signified that entire holiness, that thorough sanctification. {1Th 5:23}",
     "anchor": "Wash the inwards of him.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Th 5:23",
       "ref": "1TH.5.23"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.18",
   "range": "EXO.29.18",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "bc80f2bd",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.18#p1-bc80f2bd",
     "text": "See Rom 12:1, {See Trapp on \"Rom 12:1\"}",
     "anchor": "The whole ram.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Rom 12:1",
       "ref": "ROM.12.1"
      },
      {
       "text": "Rom 12:1",
       "ref": "ROM.12.1"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.19",
   "range": "EXO.29.19",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "08e31bcb",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.19#p1-08e31bcb",
     "text": "Both their hands between the horns of the ram.",
     "anchor": "Put their hands."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.20",
   "range": "EXO.29.20",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "b1283b8d",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.20#p1-b1283b8d",
     "text": "To set the holy obedience required of them in all senses, actions, and motions. {Joh 13:5-6; Joh 13:9}",
     "anchor": "Upon the tip of the right ear.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Joh 13:5-6",
       "ref": "JHN.13.5-6"
      },
      {
       "text": "Joh 13:9",
       "ref": "JHN.13.9"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.21",
   "range": "EXO.29.21",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "a06044db",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.21#p1-a06044db",
     "text": "Signifying Christ’s merit and Spirit.",
     "anchor": "Of the blood, and of the anointing oil."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.22",
   "range": "EXO.29.22",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "6fe02a68",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.22#p1-6fe02a68",
     "text": "A thank offering to God for advancing Aaron to the priesthood. See the like in St Paul, 1Ti 1:12.",
     "anchor": "A ram of consecration.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ti 1:12",
       "ref": "1TI.1.12"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.23",
   "range": "EXO.29.23",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "59df3281",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.23#p1-59df3281",
     "text": "See 1Co 5:7-8. {See Trapp on \"1Co 5:7\"} {See Trapp on \"1Co 5:8\"}",
     "anchor": "Unleavened bread.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Co 5:7-8",
       "ref": "1CO.5.7-8"
      },
      {
       "text": "1Co 5:7",
       "ref": "1CO.5.7"
      },
      {
       "text": "1Co 5:8",
       "ref": "1CO.5.8"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.24",
   "range": "EXO.29.24",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "2cb791d1",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.24#p1-2cb791d1",
     "text": "As acknowledging God’s omnipresence: and that many should come from east, west, north, and south, to partake of the merits and benefits of Christ, our true Sacrifice.",
     "anchor": "And shalt wave them."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.25",
   "range": "EXO.29.25",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "ff6a59eb",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.25#p1-ff6a59eb",
     "text": "Christ in like sort having offered himself for a burnt offering, for a sweet savour before the Lord, ascended up into heaven, and gave gifts unto men.",
     "anchor": "It is an offering made by flre."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.26",
   "range": "EXO.29.26",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "72e42f4e",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.26#p1-72e42f4e",
     "text": "Because he did for this time extraordinarily execute the priest’s of office.",
     "anchor": "It shall be thy part."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.27",
   "range": "EXO.29.27",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "1be85d30",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.27#p1-1be85d30",
     "text": "To teach the priests to serve the Lord with all their heart, and with all their strength.",
     "anchor": "The breast of the wave offering, and the shoulder."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.28",
   "range": "EXO.29.28",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "443e5ffc",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.28#p1-443e5ffc",
     "text": "Signifying the heaving of Christ upon the cross, and the heaving up of our hearts to God for so great benefits.",
     "anchor": "A heave offering."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.29",
   "range": "EXO.29.29",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "540e2e83",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.29#p1-540e2e83",
     "text": "Shall be his sons’ after him.] His garments remained for ever; so doth the robe of Christ’s righteousness. {Isa 61:10}",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Isa 61:10",
       "ref": "ISA.61.10"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.30",
   "range": "EXO.29.30",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "ff7013a1",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.30#p1-ff7013a1",
     "text": "There were garments but for one: there is but one Mediator, the man Christ Jesus.",
     "anchor": "And that son."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.31",
   "range": "EXO.29.31",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "e47fe4b4",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.31#p1-e47fe4b4",
     "text": "i.e., The remnant of him.",
     "anchor": "And thou shalt take the ram"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.33",
   "range": "EXO.29.33",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "d8bc7ce8",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.33#p1-d8bc7ce8",
     "text": "Apply Christ’s death by faith to their own souls. {Joh 6:51}",
     "anchor": "And they shall eat those things.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Joh 6:51",
       "ref": "JHN.6.51"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.34",
   "range": "EXO.29.34",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "49919018",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.34#p1-49919018",
     "text": "The thank offering was not to be kept till the morrow, to teach us to be prompt and present in praising God and applying Christ.",
     "anchor": "Thou shalt burn the remainder."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.35",
   "range": "EXO.29.35",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "cd1fdbf7",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.35#p1-cd1fdbf7",
     "text": "To teach the priests to consecrate their whole lives to God’s service.",
     "anchor": "Seven days."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.36",
   "range": "EXO.29.36",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "a5ba0c29",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.36#p1-a5ba0c29",
     "text": "Which, as well as the creatures, may be defiled by man’s sin. {Lev 16:16}",
     "anchor": "Cleanse the altar.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Lev 16:16",
       "ref": "LEV.16.16"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.37",
   "range": "EXO.29.37",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "810fb19e",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.37#p1-810fb19e",
     "text": "See Mat 23:19. {See Trapp on \"Mat 23:19\"}",
     "anchor": "Whatsoever toucheth the altar.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mat 23:19",
       "ref": "MAT.23.19"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mat 23:19",
       "ref": "MAT.23.19"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.38",
   "range": "EXO.29.38",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "1c958538",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.38#p1-1c958538",
     "text": "When this daily sacrifice was intermitted, - as in the days of Antiochus, that little Antichrist, - they counted it an \"abomination of desolation.\" {Dan 12:11 Mat 24:15}",
     "anchor": "Day by day continually.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Dan 12:11",
       "ref": "DAN.12.11"
      },
      {
       "text": "Mat 24:15",
       "ref": "MAT.24.15"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.39",
   "range": "EXO.29.39",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "021daf89",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.39#p1-021daf89",
     "text": "These two lambs were types of the Lamb of God, taking away the sins of the world, with a commemoration of whose benefits the day was begun and ended. Wherefore, also, from David’s days and forwards, they sang the 22nd Psalm at the morning sacrifice, and the 136th Psalm at the evening.",
     "anchor": "Thou shalt offer in the morning."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.42",
   "range": "EXO.29.42",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "9fc8f534",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.42#p1-9fc8f534",
     "text": "Hence it was called \"the tabernacle of the congregation,\" because there God met them, and made a covenant with them. See Exo 40:34.",
     "anchor": "Where I will meet you.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Exo 40:34",
       "ref": "EXO.40.34"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/EXO.29.43",
   "range": "EXO.29.43",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "a9af06d7",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/EXO.29.43#p1-a9af06d7",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"2Co 6:16\"}",
     "anchor": "And I will dwell.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "2Co 6:16",
       "ref": "2CO.6.16"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
